### 4. Competitor URL Analysis & Fact-Check

- **Supplied Competitor URL:** `https://www.caratlane.com/jewellery/jade-beads-22kt-gemstone-station-necklace-kl01354-2y00es.html`
- **Competitor Analysis Summary:**
  - *Competitor Offering:* A single e-commerce product page (22KT Jade Beads Station Necklace with 4.440 g gold weight).
  - *Identified Gaps:* Zero educational depth regarding jadeite vs nephrite distinctions, no guidance on treatment grading (Type A vs B/C), no explanation of how stone weight is deducted during gold billing, and no maintenance or styling instructions.
  - *BlueStone Differentiation:* A comprehensive 3,964-word authoritative buying guide educating buyers on mineral classification, certified Type A natural quality, protective gold mounts, statutory BIS HUID hallmarking, transparent net gold weight invoicing, and curated BlueStone gemstone jewellery designs.
- **Factual Sources & Regulations Verified:**
  - **BIS Hallmarking Standards:** Mandatory 6-digit alphanumeric HUID code, triangular BIS mark, and purity fineness stamp (750 for 18K, 916 for 22K) verifiable on the official BIS CARE mobile application.
  - **Net Gold Weight Billing:** Under Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) and Ministry of Consumer Affairs guidelines, gemstones must be weighed separately and deducted from gross weight. Jewellers cannot bill stone weight at the gold rate.
  - **GST Compliance:** Statutory 3% Goods and Services Tax applied to gold jewellery invoices in India.
  - **Gemological Standards:** Jadeite (pyroxene, Mohs 6.5–7.0) vs Nephrite (amphibole, Mohs 6.0–6.5, extreme fibrous toughness). Type A classification (untreated natural jade polished with beeswax only).

